    {
      "role": "section",
      "tag": "div",
      "cls": "Xjs2UpContainer mx-auto w-full ",
      "innerText": "Accessibility on the go With our apps, you can use text to speech and other assistive technologies to stay connected to your entertainment and in control of your home network, even when you’re not there. Groundbreaking voice control Our voice remote, available with X1 and our Flex streaming TV box, puts revolutionary accessibility features one key press or voice command away. Say “accessibility” or press B to explore all options.",
      "bg": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)",
      "color": "rgb(0, 0, 0)",
      "headings": [
        "Accessibility on the go",
        "Groundbreaking voice control"
      ]
    },
    {
      "role": "section",
      "tag": "div",
      "cls": "w-full mx-auto Xjs3UpContainer ",
      "innerText": "Comcast’s commitment Learn how Comcast NBCUniversal is committed to making our products, services, and experiences accessible to the widest possible audiences. Accessibility Support Center Reach our specially trained support team between 8 a.m. and 11 p.m. (ET), 7 days a week. Call 855-270-0379 and say \"accessibility\", send an email, use our accessible chat service, or text “Accessibility” to 266278. Xfinity Assistant Curious about an accessibility feature? Not sure how to get started? Check our online help center for more info or ask Xfinity Assistant.",
      "bg": "rgba(0, 0, 0, 0)",
